      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "What each metal steals",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "5" },
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "36" },
            { "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "34" },
            { "book": "lost-metal", "chapter": "epilogue-1" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Iron spikes steal strength, steel spikes the physical Allomantic powers, tin spikes senses, zinc spikes emotional fortitude and copper spikes mental fortitude, memory and intelligence. The Inquisitors' experiments found that atium spikes steal the temporal Allomantic powers.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "prologue" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A dead Inquisitor had a speed that was not Allomancy, and Vin finds a spike in its heart.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "5" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Spikes of other metals steal Feruchemical powers: the first Inquisitors each got a spike taken from a Feruchemist, which let them store healing.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "36" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A bronze spike driven through a Smoker's heart takes his power.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "hero-of-ages", "chapter": "34" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A trellium spike can give Allomantic and Feruchemical powers to kandra. It also lets its bearer speak to others who carry spikes, and Autonomy can act and speak through someone pierced with one.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "lost-metal", "chapter": "epilogue-1" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Beyond Scadrial",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "i-7" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "bands-of-mourning", "chapter": "epilogue" },
                { "book": "lost-metal", "chapter": "epilogue-4" }
              ]
            },
            "fires-of-december",
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "118" },
            { "book": "sunlit-man", "chapter": "epilogue" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Hemalurgy works anywhere in the cosmere, as long as there is Intent to make a spike.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "i-7" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A spike through the right eye socket can hold a Cognitive Shadow to a body in the Physical Realm, and gives that eye iron and steel sight.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "bands-of-mourning", "chapter": "epilogue" },
                { "book": "lost-metal", "chapter": "epilogue-4" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "On Miral, the Prophet bound the Megalith's soul to its body with a large silver spike and an Aon, using a buffer of Breath-like Investiture.",
          "revealedIn": ["fires-of-december"]
        },
        {
          "text": "On Roshar a variant uses crystal spikes instead of metal, in part the work of the Herald Battar. Moash had his eyes pierced by such spikes, letting him sense Investiture and see Invested beings even when they hide; like Hemalurgy, it reshapes the body so he survives.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "118" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Charred are made by piercing people with a corrupted sunheart, a cinderheart that replaces heart and lungs. It badly damages the soul and erases most memories, but gives strength, speed and toughness, making them passingly like Steel Inquisitors. If the process is interrupted, a Sunlit Charred keeps its memories and can command the others.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "sunlit-man", "chapter": "epilogue" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
